{"id":1541,"date":"2021-03-25T10:58:00","date_gmt":"2021-03-25T10:58:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?post_type=researcher&#038;p=1541"},"modified":"2025-03-16T15:16:30","modified_gmt":"2025-03-16T15:16:30","slug":"elizabeth-dadzie","status":"publish","type":"researcher","link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/researcher\/elizabeth-dadzie\/","title":{"rendered":"Elizabeth Dadzie"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover profile-banner bg-alt\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim-100 has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:none\"><\/span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\">\n\n\n<a href=\"javascript:history.back()\"> <div class=\"profiles-btn\"> \n\n<div class=\"btn-left-sq bg-primary\"> <i class=\"fa fa-caret-left white-text\"> <\/i> <\/div>\n<div class=\"btn-text title-bold white-text\">Back to Profiles<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/a>\n\n<h2 class=\"profile-name\">Elizabeth Dadzie<\/h2>\n\n<p class=\"profile-info profile-tagline primary-bold prof-pos\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span>PhD Student<\/p>\n\n<p class=\"primary-bold profile-position prof-pos\"><span class=\"primary-text is-bold\"><\/span>AIMS Ghana (Ghanaian)<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"is-layout-flow wp-block-group pad-5 profile-body\"><div class=\"wp-block-group__inner-container\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/03\/WhatsApp-Image-2025-03-07-at-12.38.48_a4f2394c.jpg\"\/>\n\n\n<p>Elizabeth Dadzie is originally from Ghana. In 2016 she got her Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Mathematics and Statistics from Methodist University College.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>In 2017, she gained admission to AIMS Ghana, where she graduated with a Master of Science in Mathematical Sciences. In 2018 she was admitted at the University of Ghana to do a Research Masters in Mathematics (MPhil Mathematics), also funded by AIMS Ghana.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>At the moment, Elizabeth is a Ph.D candidate in the Stochastic and Finance group led by Prof. Olivier M. Pamen. Her main interests are stochastic optimal control with applications in finance, data analysis and statistics.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>She\u2019s currently working on \u201cPricing and hedging weather link insurance derivatives for agricultural goods\u201d.<\/p>\n<\/div><\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Elizabeth Dadzie is originally from Ghana. In 2016 she got her Bachelor\u2019s Degree in Mathematics and Statistics from Methodist University College. In 2017, she gained admission to AIMS Ghana, where she graduated with a Master of Science in Mathematical Sciences. In 2018 she was admitted at the University of Ghana to do a Research Masters<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":4,"featured_media":12269,"parent":0,"template":"","meta":{"advgb_blocks_editor_width":"","advgb_blocks_columns_visual_guide":"","profile-researchername":"Elizabeth Dadzie","profile-researchercountry":"","profile-researcherprogram":"PhD Student"},"tags":[],"researcher_types":[41],"acf":[],"featured_img":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2021\/03\/WhatsApp-Image-2025-03-07-at-12.38.48_a4f2394c.jpg","coauthors":[],"author_meta":{"author_link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/author\/adel\/","display_name":"adel"},"relative_dates":{"created":"Posted 5 years ago","modified":"Updated 8 months ago"},"absolute_dates":{"created":"Posted on March 25, 2021","modified":"Updated on March 16, 2025"},"absolute_dates_time":{"created":"Posted on March 25, 2021 10:58 am","modified":"Updated on March 16, 2025 3:16 pm"},"featured_img_caption":"","tax_additional":{"post_tag":{"linked":[],"unlinked":[],"slug":"post_tag","name":"Tags"},"researcher_types":{"linked":["<a href=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/researcher_type\/researcher\/\" class=\"advgb-post-tax-term\">PhD Researcher<\/a>"],"unlinked":["<span class=\"advgb-post-tax-term\">PhD Researcher<\/span>"],"slug":"researcher_types","name":"Researcher Type"}},"series_order":""